  "findings": [
    "State-input equality constraints account for 34.08% of the seven intermediate child CPU durations; dynamics 25.60%, cost 22.83%, precomputation 15.60%.",
    "Projection adds 13.89% of the measured exclusive-stage CPU denominator and is outside the seven-child denominator.",
    "This profile identifies several material contributors rather than one dominant dynamics-only hotspot.",
    "Shared all-foot AD/kinematics caching, Pinocchio update reuse and collision-data allocation reuse are unimplemented candidates; no speedup was demonstrated."
  ],
  "validation": [
    "Profiling object compiled successfully from a generated vendor-source copy, retaining its original license notice.",
    "Scope self-test verified an in-flight excluded node remains excluded after begin, worker-local counters survive worker exit, and all seven child counts sum correctly.",
    "Seven intermediate child counts equal 100209; both worker TIDs observed on CPUs 6/7 with advancing CPU ticks.",
    "4999 estimates, policies and solver-health samples valid; four policies exceeded the 40 ms age ceiling, so only 4995 WBC executions were valid."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Generated copy of unchanged vendor transcription math with inserted scope timers; production archives/plugins are untouched.",
    "Accumulated wall time sums overlapping workers and must not be interpreted as SQP elapsed wall time or CPU utilization.",
    "Thread CPU time separates time executing from scheduler preemption but includes instrumentation overhead.",
    "Inclusive intermediate totals overlap their seven child stages and are excluded from fraction denominators.",
    "The denominator excludes SQP scheduling, metrics, vector moves, horizon allocation, QP and line search.",
    "Clock reads and counter bookkeeping add overhead; use an uninstrumented run for end-to-end timing.",
    "Final in-flight solve is drained before counters are collected; warmup is excluded when begin is called after initialization.",
    "Synthetic stationary inputs establish a profiling workload, not dynamic motion performance or control stability.",
    "Single short stationary synthetic-input run; planned contact scheduling can still differ across horizon nodes.",
    "A solver-healthy sample does not prove full SQP convergence, feasibility margins in dynamic motion or physical robot stability.",
    "Four policy-age violations occurred; this instrumented run is not a passed real-time or motion acceptance test.",
    "CPU frequency was observed, not forced: policy6 stayed at 2.4 GHz in sampled measurement epochs, while policy4 ranged 0.6..2.4 GHz. FIFO permission remained denied; no fixed-governor/FIFO comparison was achieved.",
    "Cost timing combines tracking and self-collision; its internal split has not been measured."
  ],
